## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design stable prompts across models and languages with guardrails.

## Key Concepts
- Prompt contracts, per-model templates, and intent extraction
- Drift testing and edge-case handling for ambiguity
- Guardrails and multilingual normalization
- Minimal prototype demonstration

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal prototype sketch
function routePrompt(userInput, context) {
  const templates = {
    en: { default: 'Template_EN' },
    fr: { default: 'Template_FR' }
  };
  const model = context.model || 'default';
  const lang = context.lang || 'en';
  const chosen = (templates[lang] && templates[lang].default) || templates['en'].default;
  const finalPrompt = chosen + '\n' + userInput;
  return { template: chosen, finalPrompt, guardrail: 'none' };
}
```

